COMM 39K(p,gamma)40Ca three-step gamma cascade scan -- 2D grid of two
COMM fictional intermediate levels, TERMINATING AT THE REAL 0+_2 STATE
COMM (~3352.6 keV, the well-known 4p-4h intruder/deformed-band-head
COMM state) instead of true ground -- see
COMM reactions/k39pg_40ca_cascade0p2_01_0100keV.reaction for the full
COMM RECL-mass-excess-shift rationale (0+ -> 0+ is single-photon
COMM forbidden, so the 0+_2 state is this cascade's own terminus, not a
COMM level with its own further gamma decay). Same 2D-grid convention as
COMM reactions/k39pg_40ca_cascade3g_*.reaction (the true-ground-state
COMM series), just in this shifted "excitation above the 0+_2 state"
COMM frame. Cascade: resonance -> Level2 -> Level1 -> the 0+_2 state,
COMM three gammas per event (100% branching at each step). Resonance
COMM excitation above the 0+_2 state: Ex - E(0+_2) = 8.93377 - 3.3526 =
COMM 5.58117 MeV. Level1 ranges 0.1 MeV up to (Level2's own cap minus
COMM 0.1 MeV); Level2 ranges from (Level1 + 0.1 MeV) up to 5.4 MeV
COMM (5.58117 - 0.1, rounded down to the 0.1 MeV grid) -- the same cap
COMM the single-level 0+_2 series itself used.
COMM
COMM THIS FILE: Level1 = 0.1000 MeV, Level2 = 2.9000 MeV (both
COMM excitation above the 0+_2 state). Gamma energies (before
COMM recoil-kinematics corrections): gamma1 = 5.58117 - Level2 =
COMM 2.6812 MeV (resonance -> Level2), gamma2 = Level2 - Level1 =
COMM 2.8000 MeV (Level2 -> Level1), gamma3 = Level1 = 0.1000 MeV
COMM (Level1 -> the 0+_2 state). Every event emits exactly three gammas
COMM -- verify with `--reaction-stats <this file>`.
COMM
COMM Both intermediate levels' lifetimes below are placeholders
COMM (1e-12 s), fictional like the levels themselves and unused by the
COMM kinematics (see ReactionConfig.hh's own LEVL card comment).

BEAM 19  39   -33.8072      # Z A massExcessMeV -- 39K
TARG 1   1    7.28897       # 1H (target, at rest)
RECL 20  40   -31.4934   8  # 40Ca -- massExcess SHIFTED to the 0+_2 state; see COMM above
ERES 0.606                  # CM resonance energy above threshold, MeV (unaffected by the RECL shift)

LEVL   1   0.1000   1.0E-12   # fictional lower intermediate level, above the 0+_2 state
LEVL   2   2.9000   1.0E-12   # fictional upper intermediate level, above the 0+_2 state

BRAT   -1  100.0   2        # resonance -> upper intermediate, 100%
BRAT    2  100.0   1        # upper intermediate -> lower intermediate, 100%
BRAT    1  100.0   0        # lower intermediate -> the 0+_2 state ("ground" in this file), 100%
SENT
